  "id": "DrugBank_DB08949 - MONDO_19975",
  "verbalization": "Inositol Nicotinate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Pellagra through a chain of indications that connect it to Beriberi and Nicotinyl Alcohol, which in turn links to Pellagra. The evidence suggests that Inositol Nicotinate may act as a precursor or mediator in the metabolic pathway leading to Pellagra, particularly through its role in the development of Beriberi. This relationship is supported by the indirect indication links, which imply that Inositol Nicotinate may influence the metabolic processes that ultimately lead to Pellagra. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Inositol Nicotinate could contribute to the development of Pellagra, though the exact nature of its involvement remains to be fully elucidated.",
